{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded","id":914261,"title":"distinction between Exigents and God-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-14T12:12:40-07:00","id":914261,"title":"distinction between Exigents and God-Blooded","content":"Is it just that God-Blooded are the literal biological children of gods and humans, while Exigents are divinely inspired by the gods in a manner similar to Exaltation, or is there something else I'm missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:15:16-07:00","id":914265,"title":"","content":"The Exigents are Exalted, they have been impowered by a sizable chunk of divine might crystallized into an exaltation by UCS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11915-wandering-swordman","name":"Wandering Swordman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11915_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:31:17-07:00","id":914278,"title":"","content":"Exigents are exalts. Some are made cooperatively with a god, others end up getting their exaltations from Games and/or black market. The power levels of exigents also vary wildly they can be as strong as &quot;terrestrial&quot; or Solar exalts. Two exigents from the same god can have totally different powers and abilities.<br /> An exigent is not necessarily considered an Anathema too, depending on which god they represent, where they are from etc...<br /> <br /> God-blooded are mortals with some powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T13:18:54-07:00","id":914319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded?p=914278#post914278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents are exalts. Some are made cooperatively with a god, others end up getting their exaltations from Games and/or black market.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the term &quot;black market exaltation&quot; referred to how GODS could acquire exaltations through some kind of divine black market (instead of directly from UCS), rather than mortals getting them for themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T13:33:40-07:00","id":914328,"title":"","content":"One big difference is that an Exigent represents a major investment for the god in question, they give up quite a bit of their life-force to channel the Exigence and it often proves fatal with even major gods being severely drained by trying to create more than one.<br /> <br /> God-blooded on the other hand dont really require anymore effort than the initial conception (I doubt female spirits have anything resembling our gestation times unless they want to be dramatic about it). A god can have a literal legion of their offspring running around or just have one whose name they cant even be bothered to remember. <br /> <br /> They are also usually meant to serve as tools or agents. An Exigent is a much more valuable asset that only the most suicidal spirit would attempt to use as a tool and they are also not in anyway expendible since there is no guarantee they reincarnate and you dont get your invested power back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T13:40:35-07:00","id":914333,"title":"","content":"They are also higher risk since it's possible for some beings to hijack the exaltation and either tamper with it or make off with it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:47:12-07:00","id":914390,"title":"","content":"The developers have said encouraging things about god blooded having a different feel to them than Exalted rather than the difference being their inferiority.<br /> <br /> In 2e if you wanted to play Runs With Bulls the daughter of Ahlat you were encouraged to pick her powers from the generic spirit charms in RoGD1 and tailor them to themes of bulls and southern warfare thus if you were creative the apple could fall very far from the tree, the problem with this was that her powers felt more inspired by Ahlat than derived from Ahlat which became evident and a bit of a problem when you wanted her to have adventures with Beacon of Power the demon blooded son of Ligier who had exactly the same list of charms to pick from and reflavour.<br /> <br /> In 3e Runs With Bulls seems like she'll be limited to what Ahlat's charms can actually do because there's not going to be a universal spirit charmset, so she'll probably have to develop a MA or a spell if she wants supernatural powers that Ahlat doesn't posess. However the advantage to that is that Beacon of Power will probably have very different charms to her so the interplay there should be more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:52:21-07:00","id":914435,"title":"","content":"I guess though, one thing about 3e, is the idea is that Charms are not literal powers that characters have, and are just representations. So Ahlat's Charms are only really shorthand for what he can do, and it's not like, &quot;Oh, here's this Exigent of Ahlat, here's Ahlat's character sheet, and even though he's a Quick Character, and these are shorthand for his general divine powers in ways optimised for an antagonist, the God Blooded can only pick off what's on the sheet&quot;, that strictly. Even though, yes, God Blooded capabilities we can expect are supposed to derive from or be powers that the God parent could do, in theory (even if they aren't represented by the God's character sheet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:12:15-07:00","id":914472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded?p=914435#post914435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess though, one thing about 3e, is the idea is that Charms are not literal powers that characters have, and are just representations. So Ahlat's Charms are only really shorthand for what he can do, and it's not like, &quot;Oh, here's this Exigent of Ahlat, here's Ahlat's character sheet, and even though he's a Quick Character, and these are shorthand for his general divine powers in ways optimised for an antagonist, the God Blooded can only pick off what's on the sheet&quot;, that strictly. Even though, yes, God Blooded capabilities we can expect are supposed to derive from or be powers that the God parent could do, in theory (even if they aren't represented by the God's character sheet).</div> </div> </div> </div>The universal charmset encouraged you to look at the charmset and then invent justifications to know the charms you wanted.<br /> Host of Spirits was as guilty as sin of this because you could lend charms to your clone(s) and thus circumvent 1 charm per action limitation on god blooded. So back when I first designed Runs With Bulls for a 2e game which never got off the ground, I justified this charm in the form of a magical bull stampede which isn't terrible (the fact she'd have been putting her attack charms into magic bulls that come from nowhere is pretty dumb but the imagery of a daughter of Ahlat calling forth a stampede is neat) but shows the kind of thematic stretching that the old model encouraged and how it could lead to homogenisation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:56:32-07:00","id":914501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded#post914261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just that God-Blooded are the literal biological children of gods and humans, while Exigents are divinely inspired by the gods in a manner similar to Exaltation, or is there something else I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, yes.<br /> <br /> Exigents are likely generally more powerful too. Most god-bloods may not even have a charmset (so much as some merits and high stats).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:53:15-07:00","id":914550,"title":"","content":"While the spirit charmset was understood to be something of a shorthand to be customized according to a certain spirit's themes and personality, the lack of an actual framework to help in directing and somehow establishing limitations one's extrapolation of such themes represented something of a complication in that it left things to open to &quot;creative abuse&quot; and a consequent potential of homogenization back into their generic basic state.<br /> <br /> In my own games i ended up developing some sort of framework, based in some extrapolation around MA charms and exalted charmsets, to actually help out with better defining the kind of places one might go with a spirit's themes, power level and such - in fact i did it partly to tinker with the idea of certain gods or other beings playing at the same as the Deathlords or the Reclamation with Abyssals &amp; Infernals respectively, among other things.<br /> <br /> What i have read here and there in the forums gives me hope that the Exigents and their systems might be 3e's way of giving us a sort of dynamic framework to the construction of both brand new exalts, that might or not be actual exigents, and the cosmic/mythic forces, personified or not, that shape the themes of their majesty &amp; might.<br /> <br /> How will this relate or not to god-bloodes, what differences or similarities might come out of it, i guess it will be a matter of wait and see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-14-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T21:00:47-07:00","id":914642,"title":"","content":"God-Blooded are luck of the draw. If you give birth to a psychopathic slavering monster, well, that monster now has power. Like monarchies, you know?<br /> Exigents can be selected, urgently or cautiously, tested for whatever criteria is important to the god.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why &quot;Chosen One&quot; is the archetypal title of a hero, and &quot;Heir&quot; is not.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason that the Realm is so worried about Anathema...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 06-15-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T05:13:03-07:00","id":914758,"title":"","content":"Yes, the matter of inherited x bestowed might is a major diferential between god-bloods and Exigents, even though the power of both would derive from the gods.<br /> <br /> On the matter of how to portray them mechanically and at the same time make them different from Exigents, one idea that has crossed my mind is adapting the old (and terribly wonky) Inheritance background as a sort of &quot;innate artifact&quot; of the god-blooded, with its powers as Evocations and the merit level defining one's range, much like with an artifact.<br /> <br /> How does that sound for a &quot;quick solve/patch&quot; of sorts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T05:28:33-07:00","id":914766,"title":"","content":"Not very helpful - dots in Artifact don't set the range of Evocations in one's artifact, other than three dots being the minimum for Evocations, period.<br /> <br /> Also it either becomes one of those &quot;the ST assigns it to everyone for free&quot; options (in which case, &quot;Merit&quot; may not be the most fitting word), or every prospective God-Blooded player will have the Merit on his sheet at five dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-15-2016, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:49:46-07:00","id":915057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded?p=914766#post914766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not very helpful - dots in Artifact don't set the range of Evocations in one's artifact, other than three dots being the minimum for Evocations, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that is pretty weird as not only i was quite certain of there being such a thing in the corebook, but feels like something that should be in there, to help STs and players with gauging artifact power level in the first place. But yeah, a lack of such info does terribly shoot down my intent. Where did i read the damn thing about evocations per level of artifact in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded?p=914766#post914766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it either becomes one of those &quot;the ST assigns it to everyone for free&quot; options (in which case, &quot;Merit&quot; may not be the most fitting word), or every prospective God-Blooded player will have the Merit on his sheet at five dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you are going and certainly have a point, but not every player in a game ever will start with Artifact 5 just because they can.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:01:40-07:00","id":915061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded?p=915057#post915057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, that is pretty weird as not only i was quite certain of there being such a thing in the corebook, but feels like something that should be in there, to help STs and players with gauging artifact power level in the first place. But yeah, a lack of such info does terribly shoot down my intent. Where did i read the damn thing about evocations per level of artifact in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guessed it from the example artifacts. The five dots have a huge range and power in their evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:22:00-07:00","id":915073,"title":"","content":"The Devs/Writers at one point came out with a <b>very vague</b> scale of power for evocations based on dots. 3 dots were mostly small, internal benefits, while 5 were huge, sweeping displays of power, and 4 is somewhere in the middle. I do not have a quote, but yeah guidelines for those are meant to be in the Arms of the Chosen book, which is next up for release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:35:18-07:00","id":915087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914261-distinction-between-exigents-and-god-blooded?p=914766#post914766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">dots in Artifact don't set the range of Evocations in one's artifact</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll probably never get a three-dot daiklave that tops out at immolating an area the size of a small city, and five-dot Artifacts seem to consistently go for higher things than hitting a single opponent who is right in front of you with a tactically significant but less than devastating elemental effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T15:22:25-07:00","id":915129,"title":"","content":"I worded that poorly, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> - you're not wrong, but the distinction is still a little on the fuzzy side, it's not telling you how many Charms/Evocations you'd have access to (indeed, some Artifacts don't get Evocations at all, even at five dots), et cetera. <br /> <br /> It's great for giving the Artifact Merit a broad range to fill, but I'd think it'd be pretty awful to mechanically base an entire splat's chargen rules off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}